Infants with transient tachypnea of the newborn present within the first few hours of life with tachypnea
  and other signs of respiratory distress, increased oxygen requirement, and ABGs that do not reflect carbon dioxide retention

Noninfectious acute respiratory disease develops in approximately 1% of all newborn infants and results in admission to a critical care unit. Transient tachypnea of the newborn is the result of a delay in clearance of fetal lung liquid. 
30% 出生前(owing to changes in the ENaC)
30% during labor (catecholamine surge)
30% 出生後(active crying and breathing)

Presentation:
The maternal history in transient tachypnea of the newborn (TTN) consists of cesarian delivery without labor or precipitous delivery. 
Signs of respiratory distress (eg, tachypnea, nasal flaring, grunting, retractions, hypoxia, increased oxygen requirement and cyanosis in extreme cases) become evident shortly after birth.  
The disorder is indeed transient, usually resolved within 72 hours after birth

Differential Diagnoses
 Cerebral Hyperventilation
 Congenital Heart Disease
 Congenital Pneumonia
 Meconium Aspiration Syndrome
 Metabolic Acidosis
 Neonatal Sepsis
 Persistent Newborn Pulmonary Hypertension
 Pneumomediastinum
 Pneumothorax Imaging
 Respiratory Distress Syndrome

Tx:
 supportive care with oxygen and NG/OG feeding<br><br>## Swallowing facilitation<br><pre class="a-b-r-La" style="user-select: text; font-family: &quot;Courier New&quot;, Courier, monospace, arial, sans-serif; line-height: normal; white-space: pre-wrap; overflow-wrap: break-word; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-size: 14px;">Oral motor: mild weak 
 Sucking power: weakness (每次吸的力量夠不夠大，應該不太容易抽出)

 Endurance: 應該要可以連續吸10下以上

 Coordination: related to breathing (如果不好，就會容易溢奶，或是容易嗆咳)
 Less swallowing movement was noted during feeding milk 
 Feeding milk 25-30 cc --&gt; taking about 30 mins    
 Limbs activity: fair

Goal: improve sucking power, sucking and swallowing coordination

PT: massage + therapeutic exercise (oral cavity)</pre></pre></span></div></span></pre></pre></pre></div></span></pre></div>